infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Where the auth state lives decides everything
  desc Sessions keep the truth on the server (revocable); a JWT keeps it in the token (valid until exp)
  compares
    - label Stateful sessions
      children
        - label State on the server
          desc Login writes a session row to Redis/DB; the cookie holds only an opaque id
        - label 1 store read per request
          desc A guard looks the session up to resolve who you are
        - label Revoke = delete the row
          desc Next lookup misses — instant, global logout on every device
        - label Needs a shared store
          desc Sticky sessions or a central Redis across every instance
        - label Fits banking & admin
          desc Server-rendered apps where kill-access-now must be instant
    - label Stateless JWT
      children
        - label State in the token
          desc The signed claims (sub, roles, exp) are the identity
        - label 0 lookups, local verify
          desc Check signature + exp, trust the payload — no I/O
        - label Un-revocable until exp
          desc No row to delete; clearing the cookie can't recall a stolen copy
        - label Shares nothing, scales out
          desc Horizontal scale with no central store on the hot path
        - label Force-logout needs state back
          desc Short TTL plus a denylist or per-user tokenVersion
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
